 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "현재완료 + already / yet / just",
   "en": "present perfect with already, yet and just"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "already는 '이미', yet은 '아직'(부정·의문문), just는 '방금'이라는 뜻으로 현재완료(have / has + 과거분사)와 함께 씁니다. already와 just는 have와 과거분사 사이에, yet은 문장 끝에 둡니다.",
   "en": "With the present perfect (have / has + past participle): already = earlier than expected, yet = until now (negatives and questions), just = a moment ago. Already and just go between have and the past participle; yet goes at the end."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "already",
     "I have already done my homework."
    ],
    [
     "yet",
     "I haven't eaten lunch yet. Have you eaten yet?"
    ],
    [
     "just",
     "He has just arrived."
    ],
    [
     "대답 / answers",
     "Yes, I have. / No, not yet."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "already / just는 have 다음, yet은 문장 맨 끝.",
    "en": "already / just after have; yet at the end."
   },
   {
    "ko": "yet은 부정문과 의문문에 씁니다.",
    "en": "Use yet in negatives and questions."
   },
   {
    "ko": "과거분사: do → done, buy → bought, eat → eaten.",
    "en": "Past participles: do → done, buy → bought, eat → eaten."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
